  "lpa_name": "Enfield",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by virtue of its insufficient provision of private amenity space, inadequate internal ceiling heights, lack of natural light to bedroom 2 of Unit 4, and unacceptable outlook and privacy for Units 1, 2 and 4,  would result in a substandard and inappropriate form of residential accommodation which would be incapable of meeting the reasonable needs of future occupiers. The proposal is therefore contrary to Chapter 14 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2026), Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021), CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD8, DMD9 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014) and the London Housing Supplementary Planning Guidance (2016).",
    "In the absence of sufficient information, the applicant has failed to demonstrate that the proposed development would provide safe and convenient pedestrian access to the site for future residents, visitors, and servicing requirements. The proposal is therefore contrary to Chapter 15 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2026); Policies T2, T3, T4 and T7 of the London Plan (2021); Policies CP24 and CP25 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010); and Policy DMD47 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed development, in the absence of adequate waste storage would fail to provide a convenient and accessible facility for managing waste generated by the development. The proposal is therefore contrary to Chapter 15 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2026), Policies T4 and T7 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP22 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010) Policies DMD30, DMD47 and DMD48 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014) and the Enfield Waste and Recycling Storage Planning Guidance (2020).",
    "The applicant has failed to provide sufficient evidence, including a robust on street parking stress survey, to demonstrate that the net increase in parking demand arising from the intensified use of the site can be accommodated without resulting in unacceptable parking stress or adverse impacts on the operation and safety of the surrounding highway network. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policy T2 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy DMD45 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014)."
  ],
